  "## What this session did

A `git cleanup conflict` pass over the superproject and its 4,316 child checkouts.
Everything below is landed on a default branch unless it says otherwise.

### Landed

| where | what |
|---|---|
| root `1e0291eff6ae` | rescued a stranded fleet-ci receipt + fixed the observatory evidence drop |
| root `da9812a13bdb` | COFOG 072 + 033 coverage entries rescued from six dead scout branches |
| root `2b5e7dab6a51` | hourly observatory run carrying the first evidence row |
| `cloud-itonami/animeka#7` | 1 untracked file |
| `cloud-itonami/eigyo-list#1` | 24 city receipt EDNs + 2 journal entries |
| `cloud-itonami/eigyo-list#2` | the append-only journal delta (disposition recorded on the PR) |
| `net-kotobase/control-plane#578` | 1 untracked file |

Retired: 21 merged remote branches, 10 local, all archived first to
`.git/stash-archive-20260830/` (348K) with an `index.txt`. Preserved by publishing,
never merged: 5 branches that existed only on this machine.

## The finding

Four separate checks this session could not make the measurement they claimed, and
each returned the value that means `fine`. This is exactly the class ADR-2608136000
names, so the point of this ADR is not the class but that it recurred four times in
one day across four unrelated tools.

### 1. An observatory mitigation that never once fired

`scripts/observatory-run.cljs` has returned `:signal` / `:load1-before` /
`:load1-after` / `:timeout-ms` from `run-one` since 2026-08-13, in a commit whose own
message is `observatory: record the load, because three timeouts today were my own
parallelism`. `datom` was ready to write all four. The record assembled between the
two never carried them, so `git log -S killed-by-signal` over
`90-docs/observatory/observatory.datoms.edn` returns no commit in the file's history.

It cost precisely what that commit predicted. At `2026-08-30T01:35:08.532Z` six
observatories (watari, mitooshi, com-etzhayyim-mikurabe, com-etzhayyim-kawaraban,
hirameki, hayari) were written `:known-broken` / `meets-expectation false` after
603-663s against the registry's 600000ms timeout, at one timestamp, on one machine.
One saturated batch, killed. In the ledger it is indistinguishable from six actors
that regressed. Those rows were not landed. The fix carries the four fields; the next
tick produced the first row in the file's history to have any of them: `meyasu`,
`load1-before 400.96`.

The lesson is narrower than 'add the field'. The field WAS added. What was missing is
that nothing ever asserted the field arrived, so a mitigation sat inert for 17 days
looking exactly like a mitigation that works.

### 2. `west-triple-sync plan --names` reads directory names, not remotes

Asked to plan registration for six paths that `cleanup-land` reported as
west-unregistered, the plan proposed three `:register` actions and three
`report-skip`s reading `GitHub repo missing: network-awai/local-murakumo-fastmtp (use
new-project-scaffold to create)`.

All six already resolve to repos west carries:

| path | remote resolves to | already in west as |
|---|---|---|
| `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kizashi` | `etzhayyim/actor-kizashi` | `orgs/etzhayyim/actor-kizashi` |
| `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-ossekai` | `etzhayyim/actor-ossekai` | `orgs/etzhayyim/actor-ossekai` |
| `orgs/network-awai-worktrees/cloud-itonami-slogan` | `network-awai/cloud-itonami` | `orgs/network-awai/cloud-itonami` |
| `orgs/network-awai/local-murakumo-fastmtp` | `network-awai/local-murakumo` | `orgs/network-awai/local-murakumo` |
| `orgs/network-awai/local-murakumo-runpod5090` | `network-awai/local-murakumo` | `orgs/network-awai/local-murakumo` |
| `orgs/network-awai/network-isekai-playtest` | `network-awai/network-isekai` | `orgs/network-awai/network-isekai` |

Every successor is checked out locally. The first two are `:renamed-upstream`, which
the cleanup runbook's own table marks `Do not re-register`. Applying the plan would
have registered two dead names, added an entry whose `:org` is
`network-awai-worktrees` (a local worktree directory, not a GitHub org), and followed
that `use new-project-scaffold to create` sentence into creating three repos that
exist. That sentence is the trap ADR-2608230300 documents by name.

`west-orphan-audit` resolves the git remote and reports `true-orphan-git=0` /
`renamed-UNVERIFIED=0`, exit 0, on the same tree. **Where the two disagree, the audit
is right.** Nothing was registered; `manifest/` was not written.

### 3. The primary-remote fallback picks the annex special remote

72% of `orgs/` checkouts have no `origin`. A fallback of `git remote | head -1` picks
`b2` — the Backblaze annex special remote — wherever it exists, because it sorts
first. Measured against `b2`, `gftdcojp/m365-archive`'s `agent/multi-mailbox-ingest`
read ABSENT-on-remote when it was already on `github/`, and a branch archive came out
`0 commits, 0B` because `$REM/main` did not resolve. Both are the silent shape: a
push that was already done reads as un-pushed work, and an archive that measured
nothing reads as an empty branch. Prefer `origin`, then a remote whose URL contains
`github.com`, and never a bare `head -1`.

### 4. `$?` after a pipe, and a waiter that waited on itself

Two shell-level instances, both already warned about in CLAUDE.md and both committed
anyway:

- `timeout 110 nbb ... > log; echo EXIT=$?` correctly reported `EXIT=124`. The same
  measurement piped to `tail` would have reported 0. Long checks go to a file first.
- `until ! pgrep -f 'cleanup-land.cljs'; do sleep; done` never exits, because the
  waiter's own command line contains that string. Four waiters hung on themselves
  before this was noticed; the fix is to capture the real PID and use `kill -0`.

## Adjacent, and unrelated to the class

**A revert caught before it shipped.** `network-awai/cloud-murakumo` held
`public/go.html` at +33/-224. That checkout is one commit behind, and the commit it
lacks (`c63bfd2`, PR #148) touches that same file: the public operator and contact
disclosure. Not landed, no PR opened, archived with the measurement under
`.git/stash-archive-20260830/child-repos/`.

**A branch that could not be preserved under its own name.**
`kotoba-lang/kotoba` `agent/guest-authoring-maturity-l2` is diverged 117 local-only /
2 remote-only. Pushed as `agent/guest-authoring-maturity-l2-local-20260830`; the
original ref is untouched. Force-push stays forbidden, so resolving the divergence is
the owning session's call.

**The west-pin guard denies the whole Bash call.** It is a PreToolUse hook, not a git
hook, so a `fetch && merge --ff-only && push` chain never runs its own sync — the
command is rejected before its first word and the checkout stays as stale as it was.
`WEST_PIN_VERIFY_SKIP=1` as a command prefix cannot reach it for the same reason. The
pin it flagged was never anything the branches did: each branch's `manifest/west.yml`
was byte-identical to its own merge-base. Sync as a separate call, then push.

## Resume point

- Nothing is half-finished. Superproject clean, 0 stashes, 0 open PRs in every repo
  touched, west orphan audit exit 0.
- The dynamic confirmation of finding 1 is ongoing: every full observatory tick from
  now should carry `:observatory/load1-before` and `:timeout-ms`, and
  `:killed-by-signal` whenever `spawnSync` reports one. If a future tick writes
  `:known-broken` with those fields nil, the carrier regressed again.
- Not done, deliberately: ~23 pushed-but-un-PR'd branches across 12 child repos, plus
  a 34-branch farm on `network-awai/app-hyakka`. The owner chose preserve-only for
  this pass. The runbook gates PR-opening behind `--branches`, which is opt-in.
- Not done: the two `etzhayyim` leftover directories. The correct move is retiring the
  stale checkouts, not registering them.
- `90-docs/observatory/observatory.datoms.edn` will be dirty again within the hour.
  That is the hourly routine regenerating it, not leftover work; it lands by cleanup
  pass, not by the routine."}]
